<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?><documents xmlns:xsi = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation = "HDocumentSchema.xsd"><document type = "H"><pnldref>H8188</pnldref><english><title>Cheat at gambling</title><additionalkeywords><additionalkeyword>cheating</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>cheated</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>cheats</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>gamble</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>gambled</additionalkeyword></additionalkeywords><standardoffencewording>On **(..SPECIFY DATE..) at **(..SPECIFY TOWNSHIP..) cheated at gambling</standardoffencewording><legislation>Contrary to section 42(1)(a) and (4) of the Gambling Act 2005.</legislation><pointstoprove>date and location &lt;br /&gt;cheated at gambling</pointstoprove><investigatoractions><investigatoraction><code>IA1</code><description>Fingerprint and photograph</description></investigatoraction><investigatoraction><code>IA2</code><description>DNA Samples: If crime scene stain present - take evidential sample If no crime scene stain and DNA not confirmed on PNC - take Criminal Justice sample. If DNA confirmed on PNC - CJ sample not required</description></investigatoraction><investigatoraction><code>IA27</code><description>Confirm proposed charge is appropriately authorised (Police or CPS)</description></investigatoraction><investigatoraction><code>IA28</code><description>Ensure compliance with investigator's obligations re disclosure</description></investigatoraction><investigatoraction><code>IA29</code><description>Consider if case suitable for referral to Financial Investigation Unit and CPS for asset recovery eg confiscation order</description></investigatoraction><investigatoraction><code>IA3</code><description>Audio record interview unless exempt</description></investigatoraction><investigatoraction><code>IA4</code><description>PNC recordable</description></investigatoraction><investigatoraction><code>IA5</code><description>Submit a crime report</description></investigatoraction></investigatoractions><policeandcpschargingresponsibilities>D27968</policeandcpschargingresponsibilities><notes>(i) Section 42(2) of the Gambling Act 2005 provides that it is immaterial whether a person who cheats&lt;br /&gt;(a) improves his chances of winning anything, or &lt;br /&gt;(b) wins anything. &lt;br /&gt;(ii) Section 42(3) of the Gambling Act 2005 provides that, without prejudice to the generality of subsection (1), cheating at gambling may, in particular, consist of actual or attempted deception or interference in connection with-&lt;br /&gt;(a) the process by which gambling is conducted, or &lt;br /&gt;(b) a real or virtual game, race or other event or process to which gambling relates.</notes></english><indictment><indictmentindicator><code>N</code><description>No</description></indictmentindicator><structuredindictmentindicator><code>N</code><description>No</description></structuredindictmentindicator></indictment><other><powersofarrest>arrest without warrant</powersofarrest><modeoftrial><code>EWAY</code><description>EITHER WAY</description></modeoftrial><timelimitforprosecutions>12 months</timelimitforprosecutions><penalty>Summary: Twelve months imprisonment and/or fine not exceeding the statutory maximum&lt;br /&gt;Indictment: Two years imprisonment and/or a fine&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;Time limit for prosecutions:&lt;br /&gt;12 months &lt;br /&gt;On the 12th March 2015 the limit on fines imposed by a Magistrates’ court was removed – as such, the potential fine on summary conviction in relation to an offence committed after this date is unlimited.</penalty><geographicregion><code>GB</code><description>Great Britain</description></geographicregion></other><codes><cjsoffencecode>GA05009</cjsoffencecode><recordableonpncindicator><code>Y</code><description>Yes</description></recordableonpncindicator><pncacpooffencecode>12.5.101.1</pncacpooffencecode><notifiabletoho><code>Y</code><description>Yes</description>